WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.167
"Remember to answer truthfully," said Oz.

2
00:00:05.168 --> 00:00:07.916
"Where did you get the silver shoes?"

3
00:00:07.917 --> 00:00:11.859
"I got them from the Wicked Witch of the East," said Dorothy.

4
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.707
"My house fell on her and killed her."

5
00:00:14.708 --> 00:00:19.907
"How did that mark get on your forehead?" asked Oz.

6
00:00:19.908 --> 00:00:24.170
"That is where the Good Witch of the North kissed me," answered Dorothy.

7
00:00:24.171 --> 00:00:29.907
The eyes stared at Dorothy and said, "You answered truthfully. What do you want?"

8
00:00:29.908 --> 00:00:35.800
"I want to go home," said Dorothy. "I'm sure Aunt Em is worried about me."

9
00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:39.911
"Why should I do this for you?" asked Oz.

10
00:00:39.912 --> 00:00:45.279
"Because you are a great wizard and I am only a girl," replied Dorothy.

11
00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:50.135
"You were strong enough to kill the Wicked Witch of the East," said Oz.

12
00:00:50.136 --> 00:00:56.285
"I didn't do it," said Dorothy. "It just happened."

13
00:00:56.286 --> 00:01:01.255
"In this country you must help me before I help you," said Oz.

14
00:01:01.256 --> 00:01:04.925
"You cannot expect to get something for nothing."

15
00:01:04.926 --> 00:01:07.751
"What must I do?" asked Dorothy.

16
00:01:07.752 --> 00:01:10.970
"You must kill the Wicked Witch of the West."

17
00:01:10.971 --> 00:01:14.591
"I can't!" exclaimed Dorothy, surprised.

18
00:01:14.592 --> 00:01:18.836
"You killed the Wicked Witch of the East," said Oz.

19
00:01:18.837 --> 00:01:23.022
"You wear the silver shoes. They have powerful magic.

20
00:01:23.023 --> 00:01:25.654
There is only one Wicked Witch.

21
00:01:25.655 --> 00:01:29.957
When you can tell me she is dead, I will send you back to Kansas."

22
00:01:29.958 --> 00:01:34.020
Dorothy was disappointed and began to weep.

23
00:01:34.021 --> 00:01:40.227
"You won't see your aunt and uncle again until the Witch is dead," Oz continued.

24
00:01:40.228 --> 00:01:45.518
"Remember—the Witch is evil and should be killed. Now go!

25
00:01:45.519 --> 00:01:49.591
Don't ask to see me again. This is your quest.

26
00:01:49.592 --> 00:01:52.586
Complete it and I will see you home."

27
00:01:52.587 --> 00:01:55.094
Dorothy left the throne room.

28
00:01:55.095 --> 00:01:59.827
She was surprised to see her friends waiting for her.

29
00:01:59.828 --> 00:02:02.627
"What happened?" asked the Tin Man.

30
00:02:02.628 --> 00:02:05.636
"There is no hope," said Dorothy.

31
00:02:05.637 --> 00:02:08.973
"Oz says I must kill the Wicked Witch of the West.

32
00:02:08.974 --> 00:02:12.730
If I don't, he won't help me."

33
00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:19.000
Her friends were sad and worried because they wondered what Oz would ask them to do.

34
00:02:19.001 --> 00:02:22.511
The Scarecrow saw Oz the next day.

35
00:02:22.512 --> 00:02:28.677
"I am Oz. Who are you and why do you seek me?" asked the Wizard.

36
00:02:28.678 --> 00:02:33.467
"I am the Scarecrow, and I'm made of straw," said the Scarecrow.

37
00:02:33.468 --> 00:02:36.937
"I want a brain instead of straw in my head."

38
00:02:36.938 --> 00:02:43.127
"In this country you must help me before I help you," said Oz.

39
00:02:43.128 --> 00:02:46.168
"What must I do?" asked the Scarecrow.

40
00:02:46.169 --> 00:02:50.979
"You must kill the Wicked Witch of the West," said the Wizard.

41
00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:54.913
"You asked Dorothy to do that!" replied the Scarecrow.

42
00:02:54.914 --> 00:02:59.519
"I did," said Oz. "I don't care who kills her.

43
00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.568
Do it, and I will give you a brain."

44
00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:06.654
The Scarecrow was very disappointed.

45
00:03:06.655 --> 00:03:10.237
The Tin Man saw Oz the next day.

46
00:03:10.238 --> 00:03:16.772
"I am Oz. Who are you and why do you seek me?" asked the Wizard.

47
00:03:16.773 --> 00:03:22.872
"I am the Tin Man. I want a heart so I can love again," said the Tin Man.

48
00:03:22.873 --> 00:03:28.987
"You cannot expect to get something for nothing," said Oz.

49
00:03:28.988 --> 00:03:32.385
"What must I do?" asked the Tin Man.

50
00:03:32.386 --> 00:03:38.408
"You must kill the Wicked Witch of the West," growled Oz.

51
00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:43.140
"Help your friends in this quest, and I will give you a heart."

52
00:03:43.141 --> 00:03:48.120
The Tin Man was very disappointed so he began to weep.

53
00:03:48.121 --> 00:03:51.112
The Lion saw Oz the next day.

54
00:03:51.113 --> 00:03:57.928
"I am Oz. Who are you and why do you seek me?" asked the Wizard once again.

55
00:03:57.929 --> 00:04:00.687
"I am the cowardly Lion.

56
00:04:00.688 --> 00:04:06.180
I want courage so I am never afraid again," answered the Lion.

57
00:04:06.181 --> 00:04:12.219
"In this country you must help me before I help you," said Oz.

58
00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.987
"What must I do?" asked the Lion.

59
00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:22.629
"Bring me proof that the Wicked Witch of the West is dead, and I will give you courage," said Oz.

60
00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:25.616
The Lion ran from the room.

61
00:04:25.617 --> 00:04:29.664
Dorothy looked at her friends and asked, "What shall we do?"

62
00:04:29.665 --> 00:04:34.933
"There's only one thing to do," said the Lion.

63
00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:38.805
"We must go to the West," continued the Tin Man.

64
00:04:38.806 --> 00:04:42.768
"We must kill the Wicked Witch," finished the Scarecrow.

65
00:04:42.769 --> 00:04:46.146
"But how?" asked Dorothy nervously.

66
00:04:46.147 --> 00:04:49.261
"I don't know," answered the Scarecrow.

67
00:04:49.262 --> 00:04:52.534
"But I want a brain, and you want to go home.

68
00:04:52.535 --> 00:04:56.939
The Tin Man wants a heart, and the Lion wants courage.

69
00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:02.447
So we must complete this quest."

